{"title":"1977 IMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> be positive integers. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/d/d7d3200f508f2bf0ee872dcc13ec904170623dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5df6a591474ffd81edd37d8d9f52f6f476caa531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />, the quotient is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and\nthe remainder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Find all pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e24c43456d95b5ab8d4f2f8f85a644e98b7ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/6/a160ba4c9bf19695732a1f1d61440fb7813f3c67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q^2 + r = 1977$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/0/6608e70df526058420e2069014c39c21f1c96be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=1977-q^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/1/d612600a316ffc27d019cf68ff4f842c1e663bfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2=(a+b)q+1977-q^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"237\" height=\"19\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/5/b05486b54710371ee63a0c2aa400fc819b59b962.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q^2-(a+b)q+a^2+b^2-1977=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"269\" height=\"19\" />, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e0350c2aff0913b5d9835108a582b9b9c8fd563.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta=7908+2ab-2(a^2+b^2)\\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"257\" height=\"19\" />. Using AM-GM inequality and the fact a,b&gt;0, we have 3(a+b)^2&lt;=7908+8ab&lt;=7098+8(a+b)^2/4, it follows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/9/5c96fe78a098116f110745197b974511d15aaac9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b\\le 88$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/39593b48da87771869f50b9b8da2bd45ba91fed1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q\\le 43$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c85c4e42b1f84138670a7213f9b61e7ab34191ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=1977-q^2\\ge 128$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />, contradicting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/7/d876a6e42e3d48cd3b40a408276e7d5da58d0d01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r&lt;a+b\\le 88$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"114\" height=\"15\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/3/5f31ac960f10c58b5d01f9aa4a5ba9c879e1be60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q\\le 44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/2/8b2b86deab5879ebfad05e4229241eb454dd8069.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q^2+r=1977$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5ab5a089aa1e866a85b80927a0d7bbe7ab2a3d5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />. It follows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/67193dd3ed82a78c99bfb3ee562689e7a806910a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=41$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" />, and we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/f/3af6208e9d288d57f25417c31e45ef447f257d07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2=44(a+b)+41\\Leftrightarrow (a-22)^2+(b-22)^2=1009\\in \\mathbb{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"477\" height=\"19\" />. By Jacobi's two squares theorem, we infer that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/73789ee839ba80b48ec002da73ccbde8420b6a65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^2+28^2=1009$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"133\" height=\"16\" /> is the only representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/e/2de9bbfcce04d2a5c63f490075fc2ab4f27e5be5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1009$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> as a sum of squares. This forces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/e/88e8ee480522227b3f7e0813b3ff5b203dfada1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(a,b)=(37,50) , (7, 50)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"191\" height=\"29\" />, and permutations. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>The above solution was posted and copyrighted by cobbler.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We start like in the first solution. Replacing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36fd00c2b7318e9966473c2819804fa80ed79ad7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1977 - q^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" />, we get the\nequation in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/1/1c1d498933d35d39b5547d12251ad6d6742591c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q^2 - (a + b) q + (a^2 + b^2 - 1977) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"286\" height=\"21\" />. Since this equation\nhas real solutions, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/0789fd234bbb750273ea55890cc0ac18907e08ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a + b)^2 - 4(a^2 + b^2 - 1977) = -3a^2 + 2ab + 7908 - 3b^2 \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"473\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>The expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/6/60697946767aea9760f48f03ea8641da61df77c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3a^2 + 2ab + 7908 - 3b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"196\" height=\"18\" /> has some non-negative values, so the\nequation in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/1/c018375f7bc5920bc24368f67d41c61bd04ab09b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3a^2 + 2ab + 7908 - 3b^2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"229\" height=\"18\" /> has real roots. (Equivalently,\nwe could use the fact that the vertex of the parabola\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/6/de6fb249bc15031e91fc583acd8b05293ae7464c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -3a^2 + 2ab + 7908 - 3b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"230\" height=\"20\" /> has positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.) It follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/2/542adfcbc57d4d7a4301c0c1a474857bd601d636.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2 + 3(7908 - 3b^2) = 4(5931 - 2b^2) \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"309\" height=\"21\" />. This implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/7/b27ef64810465bbb26d2bead7495b2130f8fc3f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\le 54$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />.\nSimilarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66427f6f2778bd26b88887cd2aad7021e3aa931.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\le 54$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7ce4080141821c133fdcbd628671cda9a174a0bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1977 = q^2 + r &lt; q^2 + a + b \\le q^2 + 108$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"302\" height=\"20\" /> from which we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/888f3a814186e9f9bc46471e123ec79c6e23249a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q &gt; \\sqrt{1977 - 108}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"22\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/d/33d6a0835311992535f2c7a2187ff0cdd9444b9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q \\ge 44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />. On the other hand, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/3/9b39e6b1ea7470d5559f58b785b98f4bc6694502.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q^2 \\le 1977$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" />,\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/8/508c7daa73587980662204f5d6db15a65a030600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q \\le 44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/e/bfea4771db7d8d0f67adf350bccfba8ac7463ada.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = 44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />. This implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/3/4b3cb027441092788b155ed612bf607e9f973045.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We now have to solve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/c/aacae10b7ab46795908ecb449b1a0a4e8b6c51a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2 = 44(a + b) + 41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"193\" height=\"21\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3834f0cef2a1f4d8524aa5bc8e3faca298550862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> are positive\nintegers. As an equation in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/5/c6535998aa0e7f3075a996cd2c2a670acdd20888.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 - 44a + (b^2 - 44b - 41) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"242\" height=\"21\" />.\nWe have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/9/09993ff2b5fc8f6ae1522f22bff7f1c2d7de7825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 22 \\pm \\sqrt{484 - b^2 + 44b + 41}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"245\" height=\"21\" />. The expression under the\nsquare root has to be a square, say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/4/b8435ce3b6ca282de6981acfea331c29beb6646f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$525 - b^2 + 44b = c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />,\nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/f/92f669e3fc614730559f182f7eed990ec254bbb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b - 22)^2 + c^2 = 1009$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>We now want to find all the possible pairs of squares which add to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/e/2de9bbfcce04d2a5c63f490075fc2ab4f27e5be5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1009$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />.\nThere are 32 squares from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/4/ad4cc976db8c76bb2527332e41874839c7dba5a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaaf93d6f589f7f63bdbe8da0314dd180738540f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31^2 = 961$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" /> to be considered\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/a/52a6ab23571ecfa7cb715738d4960047704cd8b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(32^2 = 1024 &gt; 1009).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"21\" /> In looking for pairs which add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/e/2de9bbfcce04d2a5c63f490075fc2ab4f27e5be5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1009$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />, we\ncan discard the squares <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/2/b521a554a5b8e1680aab8b3d2a4f8d16e28e51ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" />. We discard <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a56ee21dfa8a7a22188996eeabf521d2346a0541.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49, 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" /> as well, since they\ncan not be used in a pair of squares which adds to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/e/2de9bbfcce04d2a5c63f490075fc2ab4f27e5be5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1009$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />. Note that the\nlast digit of squares is one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67af67d70f2be4de1041d0b128d0f1f7a8754551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 1, 4, 5, 6, 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" />. So we can discard\nsquares whose last digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and only consider pairs of squares\nwhose last digits are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The remaining squares\nwe have to consider are\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/9/e193685f0c8e411110acbc9892edeb4997d035d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100, 144, 169, 225, 324, 289, 400, 484, 529, 625, 729, 784, 900$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"453\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Let us look at the sequences <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/0/440e2470c3ae63999400c7c8842a55973db55716.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144, 225, 324, 484, 625, 784$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"206\" height=\"17\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45e426dbd392267275c806ddae9902b8913f0779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100, 169, 289, 400, 529, 729, 900$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"241\" height=\"17\" />. From each sequence choose pairs of\nnumbers which add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/e/2de9bbfcce04d2a5c63f490075fc2ab4f27e5be5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1009$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />. Obviously, the only pair is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/a/23a1ac5964009acaf1aa82d22a0a4df6fa6e946b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$225 = 15^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" />\nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/3/723e1fef2cb752186de0e5651dfe5007c9c0654e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$784 = 28^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" />. Thus, we can have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/8/868c79d7b64ee21fbceb08b6e24553f7adf32c46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b - 22 = \\pm 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/f/40f7ac40edbfb5895532386768f6b0e7554d0b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b - 22 = \\pm 28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" />.\nThis gives the possible values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/e/99e496535284d5b7f9472c58196c1bd13d31de3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 7, 37, 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />. From\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/9/09993ff2b5fc8f6ae1522f22bff7f1c2d7de7825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 22 \\pm \\sqrt{484 - b^2 + 44b + 41}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"245\" height=\"21\" /> we get the corresponding values\nfor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> (keep only the positive ones). This yields the values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e24c43456d95b5ab8d4f2f8f85a644e98b7ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />\nto be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/b/08b7ad0f8dacc52a95f9462b2dc51f6144ca771f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7, 50), (37, 50), (50, 7), (50, 37)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"242\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>[Solution by pf02, April 2026] \n</p><p><br />\nThe original thread for this problem can be found here: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c6h61028\">[1]</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO\" title=\"1977 IMO\">1977 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1977 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1977 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1977 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1977 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1977 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1977 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1977 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1977 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017065535\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.034 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.048 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 326/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 895/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 15004/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.974      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.974      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:20524:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017065535 and revision id 280770. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}